# Without this file, `docker build` sends the entire backend/ directory as
# build context on every build — including .venv/ (1.4GB+ of ML packages:
# torch, spaCy, EasyOCR), which made builds transfer a gigabyte-plus of
# local files that get reinstalled fresh inside the container anyway. This
# is what made the backend image take an extremely long time to build.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.git/
data/uploads/
*.egg-info/
